# Authentication and authorization of the services
#
# Development and tests use the mocked users viewer, agent and admin (the password is the user name);
# production uses XSUAA. Start the app with `npm run cds-watch` (http://localhost:4004).
# Without credentials a request gets 401. A user without any of the roles Viewer, Agent and Admin
# gets 403. "stranger" is such a user: the mocked authentication accepts any user name that is not
# configured, with an empty password, as a user without roles.

@host = http://localhost:4004

### No credentials
# expect: 401
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages

### Wrong password
# expect: 401
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages
Authorization: Basic viewer wrong

### A user without a role
# expect: 403
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages
Authorization: Basic stranger stranger

### The roles are named like the scopes in xs-security.json. A viewer reads...
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages?$top=1&$select=customerMessageID
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### ...but may not change anything: editing a message (which creates a draft) is refused
# expect: 403
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=08bb27b2-9357-4598-9ea3-6b9f8dcb6d99,IsActiveEntity=true)/benicio_1_04Srv.draftEdit
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "PreserveChanges": true
}

### The sample messages were created by the agent, so the agent may edit them...
# expect: 201
POST {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=08bb27b2-9357-4598-9ea3-6b9f8dcb6d99,IsActiveEntity=true)/benicio_1_04Srv.draftEdit
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "PreserveChanges": true
}

### ...and discard the draft again
# expect: 204
DELETE {{host}}/service/benicio_1_04/CustomerMessages(ID=08bb27b2-9357-4598-9ea3-6b9f8dcb6d99,IsActiveEntity=false)
Authorization: Basic agent agent
